course: dictionary
lesson: 15252
title: Shod: shoes and horseshoes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shod is an old-fashioned word, so you will mostly meet it in old stories, poems and books about horses. The words around it give you clues. «The blacksmith shod the horse before the race.» A blacksmith works with metal, and a racehorse needs shoes, so shod must mean fitted with horseshoes.
explain: «The walkers were well shod for the mountain path.» The path is rough and steep, so the walkers must have good shoes on their feet. Well shod means wearing good, strong shoes. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «The old man tapped the floor with his iron-shod stick.» Iron tells you the metal part matters here. Iron-shod means the end of the stick has a covering of metal. Shod can change its meaning a little, so look at the words next to it.
fact: Shod is the past form of the verb shoe: shoe, shoes, shod, shoeing.
fact: «The blacksmith shod the horse» means he fitted horseshoes onto the horse.
fact: «Well shod» means wearing good shoes, and «shod in» means wearing a certain kind of shoe.
fact: «Iron-shod» means having a metal end or covering.
fact: Shod is formal or old-fashioned, so it is most common in older books and poems about horses and blacksmiths.
exercise: «The blacksmith shod the horse before the race.» What does shod mean here? | *Fitted with horseshoes | Brushed and fed | Taken for a walk | Washed in the river
exercise: «The walkers were well shod for the hike.» What does well shod mean? | Carrying heavy bags | Hungry and cold | *Wearing good, strong shoes | Very tired after the hike
exercise: «The old man tapped the floor with his iron-shod stick.» What does iron-shod mean? | Painted bright red | Made of wood only | Very long and thin | *With a metal covering on its end
test: «She was shod in soft leather slippers.» What is she wearing on her feet? | Wellies | *Soft leather slippers | Snow boots | Nothing at all
test: «The stable boy said the horse was newly shod.» What does newly shod mean? | It was born only yesterday | It has been washed clean | Its shoes are new | *It has just had new horseshoes fitted
exam: Which is the past form of the verb shoe? | Shown | Shoeing | Shoes | *Shod
